    "body": "## Summary\n- require a service category id when creating a job\n- validate that the selected category exists, is active, and is a concrete leaf rather than a parent group\n- persist the category relation already introduced by Flyway V17\n- expose category id/slug/name/fulfillment mode in job responses\n- load the public hierarchical category catalog in the create-job UI\n- present grouped POINT_TO_POINT leaf categories and submit the selected category with the job\n- add focused JobService coverage for category assignment and parent-category rejection\n\n## Scope boundary\nThis PR keeps the existing A→B route-quote creation flow intact and therefore exposes only `POINT_TO_POINT` leaves in the current create-job form. `ON_SITE` categories remain in the public catalog and will get their one-location creation flow in the next atomic iteration rather than being forced into fake A→B routing.\n\n## Validation\nCI is the merge gate. Do not merge unless backend tests/build, frontend lint/build, runtime/Flyway smoke and payments-ledger smoke all pass.",
